# Codebase Memory MCP (default)

Use the `codebase-memory-mcp` project server (or `user-codebase-memory-mcp` if
the user installed it globally) **before** grep/file-by-file reads when exploring
**this** codebase.

Install (once per machine):

```bash
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DeusData/codebase-memory-mcp/main/install.sh | bash
```

`/workspace` is refused as a single index root (too broad). Index the live trees
below. Do **not** index `legacy/` (frozen Tour Ops; already in `.cbmignore`).

## Indexed projects

| Area | `project` | `repo_path` |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Packages / SDK / workspaces | `app-tour-packages` | `/workspace/packages` |
| Apps (api, web, portal, marketing) | `app-tour-apps` | `/workspace/apps` |
| Docs | `app-tour-docs` | `/workspace/docs` |
| Scripts / guards | `app-tour-scripts` | `/workspace/scripts` |
| Infra / SQL | `app-tour-infra` | `/workspace/infra` |
| Design-system tokens | `app-tour-design-system` | `/workspace/design-system` |

Pass that `project` name on every graph tool call.

## Session start

1. `list_projects` — confirm the six projects above are present.
2. If a tree is missing, `index_repository` that `repo_path` with the matching `--name`.
3. `auto_index` is enabled after install; new sessions should pick up incremental updates.

CLI equivalents (when MCP is not attached yet):

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
codebase-memory-mcp cli list_projects
codebase-memory-mcp cli index_repository --repo-path /workspace/packages --name app-tour-packages
codebase-memory-mcp cli get_architecture --project app-tour-packages
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project app-tour-packages --name-pattern '.*Handler.*' --label Function
codebase-memory-mcp cli trace_path --project app-tour-apps --function-name '<ExactName>' --direction both
```

## Tool selection

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Find definitions, classes, routes, symbols | `search_graph` |
| Text search enriched with graph context | `search_code` |
| Callers / callees / data flow | `trace_path` |
| Architecture, modules, hotspots, layers | `get_architecture` |
| Uncommitted change impact | `detect_changes` |
| Read a known symbol body | `get_code_snippet` (after `search_graph`) |
| Multi-hop graph patterns | `query_graph` |
| Coverage of cited paths | `check_index_coverage` |

## When NOT to use graph tools

- Editing a file the user already pointed to
- Config/docs-only questions with no code structure
- One-off string search in a known file path

## Fallback

If MCP is disconnected or returns empty results, use the CLI commands above, then
`Grep` / `Read`. Say that indexing or MCP attach may be pending (new Cloud Agent
sessions load `.cursor/mcp.json`; this session may need a restart).
